    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1374">

                <pb facs="1076" n="960" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg960"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.11/71.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1327.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 23, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As a result of the continued disturbed
                    state of this country the Embassy is in almost daily receipt of enquiries from
                    citizens of the United States, who have suffered loss and damage to their
                    properties, concerning what action they shall take in the matter of their claims
                    against the Government of Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to request that the Department of State instruct the Embassy in
                    the premises. At the present time I am treating these cases precisely as they
                    were treated in the last revolution.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
